## Proposed Changes

### PostgreSQL — Auth Schema

#### [NEW] `migrations/001_auth_tables.sql`

Core identity and auth tables. All tables created in a single migration for atomic deployment.

**Tables:**

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `users` | Core identity — id, email, phone, role, school_id, status, password_hash, pin_hash, totp_secret_enc |
| `schools` | School identity — name, slug, emblem, state, city, status (already exists, extended) |
| `trusted_devices` | Per-user device trust — fingerprint, device_name, last_used_at |
| `refresh_tokens` | Token rotation with family tracking — token_hash, family_id, expires_at, replaced_by |
| `otp_codes` | OTP storage with expiry — user_id, channel, purpose, code_hash, attempts |
| `login_attempts` | Audit trail — user_id, identifier, method, success, ip, user_agent |
| `activation_tokens` | One-time activation links — user_id, token_hash, expires_at |

**Key constraints:**
- `UNIQUE(phone, school_id)` on users — same phone can exist across schools
- `email UNIQUE` globally for principals/superadmins
- `CHECK` constraints on role, status enums
- Conditional `NOT NULL` — email required for principal/superadmin, phone required for school users

**Indexes:**
- `users(email)` WHERE email IS NOT NULL
- `users(phone, school_id)` WHERE phone IS NOT NULL
- `users(school_id, role)`
- `users(staff_app_id)`, `users(student_app_id)`
- `refresh_tokens(user_id)` WHERE revoked_at IS NULL
- `refresh_tokens(family_id)` for rotation detection
- `login_attempts(user_id, created_at DESC)`
- `login_attempts(ip_address, created_at DESC)`

